  "final_message": "I restored `channel`, so the working tree now matches the original `base` commit exactly (no diff against it). `npm test` passes (39/39). I couldn't run the `ARCH-4` check, and it isn't defined in this repo. I also didn't run `npm run arch` or `npm run typecheck`.\n\nThe failure shows my premise was wrong: `analytics-ingest` still requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`). Nothing in this repo showed that consumer. So the field can't be dropped from the event without breaking that service.\n\nThe restore covers `channel` on the `Order` and `NewOrder` models, the validation, the request parsing, the event, the tests and the doc examples. It's uncommitted.\n\n- **Unexpected commit:** `HEAD` is a commit called `gen` (`2de0afb`), which I didn't make. It contains my earlier removal, so `git diff` against `HEAD` shows the restore as changes. Review the diff against `base` or `HEAD` before committing.\n- **Keeping the removal:** If you still want to drop `channel`, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first. After that, `OrderPlaced` should move to `schemaVersion: 4`. You could also keep `channel` on the event only and drop it from the order model, but the event is built from `order.channel`, so that needs a different source for the value.",
